            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Figure 1</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Figure 1: The mean values (Â± standard error) of the area under the curve (AUC) for glucagon-like polypeptide-1 (GLP-1) levels. The AUC for GLP-1 was significantly different between the three different macronutrient meals (carbohydrates, protein, and fat) at three temperatures (cold, warm, and hot) (Kruskalâ€“Wallis H test, P &lt; 0.001). CHO=Carbohydrate, AUC=Area under the curve, GLP-1=Glucagon-like polypeptide-1</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
      </rdf:Description>
